From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer/explorerframe/dwmapi: taskbar thumbnails, the thumbnail toolbar, tabs and iconic bitmaps

The taskbar showed no thumbnails, and what programs give for them were
stubs: ITaskbarList3's ThumbBarAddButtons, ThumbBarUpdateButtons,
ThumbBarSetImageList and SetThumbnailTooltip "faked success",
SetThumbnailClip, the tab methods and ITaskbarList4's SetTabProperties
returned E_NOTIMPL, and DwmSetIconicThumbnail did nothing. Media players'
play/pause/next buttons under the thumbnail, browsers' and editors' tab
thumbnails were missing.

- Hovering over a window's taskbar button (400 ms) shows thumbnails
  above it (below for a bar at the top): each window of the button (all
  of a combined group's), titled with the window's title and its icon,
  showing the window as it looks -- taken from the screen, or as it last
  looked when it is minimized, the SetThumbnailClip part of it when one
  is set -- or, for a window that asked for an iconic representation
  (DWMWA_HAS_ICONIC_BITMAP / DWMWA_FORCE_ICONIC_REPRESENTATION), the
  bitmap it gives when sent WM_DWMSENDICONICTHUMBNAIL. A click brings the
  window forward; its x sends SC_CLOSE. The popup goes when the pointer
  leaves it and the button.
- The thumbnail toolbar: up to seven buttons (more is E_INVALIDARG) with
  icons (THB_ICON, or THB_BITMAP from the image list ThumbBarSetImageList
  gave) and tooltips; disabled ones are greyed, hidden ones left out,
  non-interactive ones not clickable, no-background ones drawn bare; a
  click sends the window WM_COMMAND with THBN_CLICKED and the button's
  id, and DISMISSONCLICK closes the thumbnails. ThumbBarUpdateButtons
  changes them by id, while shown. Icons travel as 32-bit bits (icon
  handles are per process).
- SetThumbnailTooltip is the thumbnail's tooltip.
- Tabs: RegisterTab, UnregisterTab, SetTabOrder, SetTabActive and
  SetTabProperties keep a window's tabs; its thumbnails are then its
  tabs, in their order, each with the iconic bitmap its proxy window
  gives; a click activates the proxy (WM_ACTIVATE) and brings its window
  forward; the x sends the proxy WM_CLOSE.
- dwmapi: DwmSetIconicThumbnail sends the bitmap to the taskbar,
  DwmInvalidateIconicBitmaps makes it forget it, and
  DwmSetIconicLivePreviewBitmap is taken (this taskbar has no peek).

Wine's explorerframe taskbarlist tests: no failures, as before.

Gate: test/thumbbar-gate.sh (the shell's desktop, test/thumbbar-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_THUMBNAILS, SG_MUTANT_NO_THUMB_CLICK
(programs/explorer/systray.c), SG_MUTANT_NO_ICONIC (dwmapi/dwmapi_main.c).
